news alert  and that breaking first at five a  shooting investigation at western high  school involving both ccsd police and  metro it is happening now near bonanza  and decatur a good evening to you on  this tuesday thank you for joining us at  five i'm brian loftis and i'm denise  valdez let's get right out to madison  kimbra who's been following the story  and has an update madison  a lot of commotion out here this area of  bonanza has been blocked off for over an  hour as you can see behind me now with  metro police and crime tape up bonanza  is closed in both directions from  decatur through estrella avenue  currently awaiting confirmation from  police on what exactly happened we did  however talk to students and parents  that say this stemmed from a student  bringing a gun to school another student  also says she heard gunshots i asked a  parent if she got any calls or email  about what happened  no we don't have any information by  email the school  is  very  proud conservative they don't share  information with parents i sent a test  to my daughter  and she already responded she said  something happened but  i don't know what happened  we are expecting police to brief at any  moment on what happened meanwhile  victoria saha is at umc talking to  people who say they were involved in the  incident victoria what can you tell us  thanks madison the family here tells me  they were not students at western high  school they were meeting up with other  students at the school that's when a  fight was about to start with another  group of students from western high  school then this group drove off then  they tell me school police surrounded  their car as they were trying to leave  the area but while they were leaving  their car moves toward police and that's  what prompted school police to draw  their weapons and shoot at the car we do  know two people were shot inside this  car a teen boy had a bullet graze his  shoulder the family tells me he is  expected to be ok 